From: zibao <zibao@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: core: stop the pretimeout hrtimer on suspend

The kernel has a software pretimeout hrtimer
(CONFIG_WATCHDOG_HRTIMER_PRETIMEOUT) beside the keepalive timer.
watchdog_dev_suspend() cancels the keepalive timer and its worker, but
leaves the pretimeout timer armed: it fires during s2idle and
pretimeout_panic() panics the kernel.

Measured on a H96 Max H618 (sunxi-wdt, s2idle, systemd RuntimeWatchdogSec
15 s): a 60 s sleep armed with rtcwake panics with "watchdog pretimeout
event".  The stack is:

  pretimeout_panic
  watchdog_notify_pretimeout
  watchdog_hrtimer_pretimeout
  __hrtimer_run_queues
  hrtimer_interrupt
  ...
  default_idle_call

Stop the pretimeout hrtimer on suspend and restart it on resume.

Signed-off-by: zibao <zibao@proton.me>

--- a/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/watchdog_dev.c
@@ -1296,6 +1296,7 @@
 	 */
 	kthread_cancel_work_sync(&wd_data->work);
 	hrtimer_cancel(&wd_data->timer);
+	watchdog_hrtimer_pretimeout_stop(wdd);
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -1319,6 +1320,8 @@
 		ret = __watchdog_ping(wd_data->wdd);
 	mutex_unlock(&wd_data->lock);
 
+	watchdog_hrtimer_pretimeout_start(wdd);
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
